{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EWwGRWAmHLRcxroMsndo1U","type":"tool_result","content":"import Mathlib\n\nopen Filter Topology\n\n/--\nSay that an $n$-by-$n$ matrix $A=(a_{ij})_{1 \\leq i,j \\leq n}$ with integer entries is \\emph{very odd} if, for every nonempty subset $S$ of $\\{1,2,\\dots,n\\}$, the $|S|$-by-$|S|$ submatrix $(a_{ij})_{i,j \\in S}$ has odd determinant. Prove that if $A$ is very odd, then $A^k$ is very odd for every $k \\geq 1$.\n-/\ntheorem putnam_2021_b5\n(n : ℕ)\n(npos : n ≥ 1)\n(veryodd : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℤ → Prop)\n(hveryodd : ∀ A, veryodd A ↔ ∀ m ∈ Set.Icc 1 n, ∀ reind : Fin m → Fin n, Function.Injective reind → Odd (A.submatrix reind reind).det)\n: ∀ A, veryodd A → (∀ k ≥ 1, veryodd (A ^ k)) :=\nsorry","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e332a210-1557-4910-a501-7b16a67c1a0f","uuid":"17f9cd40-4970-4032-bf7f-828bb63700bf","timestamp":"2026-10-14T03:10:01.935Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"import Mathlib\n\nopen Filter Topology\n\n/--\nSay that an $n$-by-$n$ matrix $A=(a_{ij})_{1 \\leq i,j \\leq n}$ with integer entries is \\emph{very odd} if, for every nonempty subset $S$ of $\\{1,2,\\dots,n\\}$, the $|S|$-by-$|S|$ submatrix $(a_{ij})_{i,j \\in S}$ has odd determinant. Prove that if $A$ is very odd, then $A^k$ is very odd for every $k \\geq 1$.\n-/\ntheorem putnam_2021_b5\n(n : ℕ)\n(npos : n ≥ 1)\n(veryodd : Matrix (Fin n) (Fin n) ℤ → Prop)\n(hveryodd : ∀ A, veryodd A ↔ ∀ m ∈ Set.Icc 1 n, ∀ reind : Fin m → Fin n, Function.Injective reind → Odd (A.submatrix reind reind).det)\n: ∀ A, veryodd A → (∀ k ≥ 1, veryodd (A ^ k)) :=\nsorry","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EWwGRWAmHLRcxroMsndo1U","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
